### Single Track Simulation, Event Mixing and Event Reconstruction

The details of single track simulation and event mixing in real data and MC embedding is explained in Ch. III Sec. A. In real data embedding, the simulated TPC ADC values of the single track event were added to those in the real data event, and then the event was constructed as if it comes from real data. In contrast, in MC embedding, the TPC responses from the single track simulation were mixed with the

