This section discusses the calculation results of TPC tracking efficiencies in both real data embedding and MC embedding, based on the datasets and analysis procedures discussed in previous chapters, for the STAR 200 GeV proton-proton longitudinal data during Run 6. In general, tracking efficiencies calculated in real data embedding are systematically lower than those calculated in MC embedding.

